At first, standing there gives you too much time to think. You hear Gwylan move behind the counter,
pick up the ledger and turn a page, but you cannot see whether <<he>> is reading or looking at you.
<br><br>
Every small sound makes you wonder if <<he>> has decided to come back.
<br><br>
A customer enters a few minutes later. You hear the door open,
then Gwylan's voice change into the easy tone <<he>> uses for business. <<He>> crosses the shop to find something,
wraps it in paper, takes the customer's coins and says goodbye without mentioning why you are standing behind the herb shelves.
<br><br>
The door closes again. Gwylan returns to the counter, and the quiet stretches on.
<br><br>
By then your calves have started to ache, so you shift your weight carefully from one foot to the other while
you wait for <<him>> to decide that <<hes>> ready.
